@pquantin, I have checked what you suggested. It does not work with bitmasks and for values above 2 bits (why 2-bits and not 1-bit or all bits for crying out loud)? 

So, it will not even work for  8-bit masks.

Code:
```
       { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[0],
            { "Controller Multi-Path I/O and Namespace Sharing Capabilities (CMIC)", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic",
               FT_UINT8, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x0, NULL, HFILL}
        },
        { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[1],
            { "Multiple Ports Support", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic.mp",
               FT_BOOLEAN, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x1, NULL, HFILL}
        },
        { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[2],
            { "Multiple Controllers Support", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic.mc",
               FT_BOOLEAN, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x2, NULL, HFILL}
        },
        { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[3],
            { "SRIOV Association", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic.sriov",
               FT_BOOLEAN, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x4, NULL, HFILL}
        },
        { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[4],
            { "ANA Reporting Support", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic.ana",
               FT_BOOLEAN, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x8, NULL, HFILL}
        },
        { &hf_nvme_identify_ctrl_cmic[5],
            { "Reserved", "nvme.cmd.identify.ctrl.cmic.rsvd",
               FT_UINT8, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0xf0, NULL, HFILL}
        },
 ```
This is what I see:
![image](/uploads/c20c90d4930aa845950bf32646bcdd59/image.png)

While with FT_UINT8 instead of FT_BOOLEAN, I see what is expected:

![image](/uploads/89020553c6702531a9600ab4cd865cf4/image.png)

So, I believe this pattern shall stay.

@pquantin, I have implemented your suggestions. Please see the top level commit.

I have used FT_BOOLEAN for previous changes as well, that are already merged.

Please do not be concerned about the following chunk (0.01 vs 0.001), it is not a typo but correct:
```
